# Declared exemptions for kz-extension-is-earned.
#
# Format: staged-path | reason
#   path   — repo-relative path of the staged .kz, exactly as git reports it
#   reason — why the facet stays even though the file carries no host
#            content. Mandatory. This file is for DELIBERATE .kz-pure files
#            (a positive test whose purpose is the .kz parse surface); the
#            mechanical cases (expected.json, MUST_ERROR, LANGUAGES,
#            input.k sibling, tests/broken) are exempted by the check
#            itself and belong nowhere here.
#
# An entry only matters while its path is staged — dormant entries are
# notes, not failures (diff-scope makes "matches no site" the normal case).

# The facet sweep's six keeps — pure by the parser, .kz by design.
koru_std/index.kz | module index — a .k index flips every .kz sibling's ~pub into KORU111 contract violations
koru_std/bridge.run.kz | part file of the bridge module — a lone .k part puts the module in contract-split mode (KORU111)
koru_std/compiler.directives.kz | part file of the compiler module — same contract-split trigger as bridge.run
koru_std/compiler.commands.kz | part file of the compiler module — same contract-split trigger as compiler.directives
koru_std/runtime.parsewire.kz | part file of the runtime module — same contract-split trigger as bridge.run
koru_std/interpreter.args.kz | part file of the interpreter module — a lone .k part puts the module in contract-split mode (KORU111)
koru_std/interpreter.defined.kz | part file of the interpreter module — same contract-split trigger as interpreter.args
koru_std/interpreter.validate.kz | part file of the interpreter module — same contract-split trigger as interpreter.args
koru_std/runtime.runcached.kz | part file of the runtime module — same contract-split trigger as interpreter.args
koru_std/bridge.affordances.kz | part file of the bridge module — decl-only after affordances-render split; a lone .k part puts the module in contract-split mode (KORU111)
koru_std/interpreter.pool.kz | part file of the interpreter module — comments-only stub after pool-organ split; same contract-split trigger as interpreter.args
koru_std/runtime.affordances.kz | part file of the runtime module — comment-only after affordances-gate split; same contract-split trigger as interpreter.args
tests/regression/100_MODULE_SYSTEM/140_FILE_LAYOUT/140_021_part_tilde_spelling/input.kz | pins host-embedded `~` part declarations — converting vacates the pin
tests/regression/200_COMPILER_FEATURES/210_PARSER/210_312_empty_source_block_eats_next_decl_kz/input.kz | the test names the .kz spelling — the bug it pins only reproduces on the host-embedded facet
tests/regression/100_MODULE_SYSTEM/140_FILE_LAYOUT/140_029_dup_tor_across_facets_refused/input.kz | the pin is facet-companion duplication itself — a .k twin changes what the test measures
koru_std/grid.kz | module root of a ~part family — `~part` is a host-switch directive and PARSE003 refuses it in a .k file; the join lines are the host content that earns the facet
